I think I have a more sadistic suggestion, unrelated to (M)MF amnesia
attacks: B/U/C status (and enchantment, for that matter) should only be
indicated at the time of discovering it, and not included in the item's
description in your inventory.  That way, dropping your unihorn on an
altar to find that it's *currently* uncursed won't allow you to know
automatically when a Lich curses it much later in the game.

But I think the main effect it would have on gameplay is to make all
games a lot more like atheist ones, where you can't use an altar to give
objects (permanently) known BUC status.


